# Strapi 5 Content API — frontend query patterns (tenant, populate, published)

Correct patterns for Strapi 5 Content API calls from Next.js (or any consumer). Incorrect syntax causes 400 Bad Request errors.

**Slug casing policy** (use `$eq` with kebab-case; `$eqi` only as legacy): see [strapi-nextjs-frontend-slug-contract-kebab-case-category-filters.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/strapi-nextjs-frontend-slug-contract-kebab-case-category-filters.mdc) and [strapi_frontend_slug_contract.md](mdc:documentation/strapi_frontend_slug_contract.md).

**Cloud tenant/category repair** (when lists return 0 despite local data): [strapi-cloud-production-news-tenant-category-slug-and-cover-repair-runbook.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/strapi-cloud-production-news-tenant-category-slug-and-cover-repair-runbook.mdc).

## Problem solved

- **status=published** – Can cause validation errors in Strapi 5; use `filters[publishedAt][$notNull]=true` instead
- **Comma-separated populate** – `populate=cover,category,author` triggers 400s; Strapi 5 expects array-style populate
- **Empty tenant lists** – Never drop the tenant filter when the API returns 200 with 0 items

## Tenant filtering (required — no fallback)

All directory and news list/detail requests **must** use the tenant filter. Display only data scoped to the current tenant.

### DO: Always filter by tenant

- **Directory** (e.g. bishops, parishes): `filters[tenant][tenantId][$eq]=${tenantId}` — no fallback. If the API returns 200 with 0 items, show 0 items.
- **News** (articles, flash-news-items, advertisement-slots): Same. Always include `filters[tenant][tenantId][$eq]=${tenantId}`. Do **not** retry without the tenant filter when the response is 200 with empty data.

### DON'T: Fall back to no-tenant when response is 200 with 0 items

```typescript
// ❌ DON'T: Retry without tenant when tenant filter returns 0 items
if (list.length === 0) {
  const noTenant = await fetch('/articles?filters[publishedAt][$notNull]=true&...');
  list = noTenant.data; // Wrong — shows other tenants' data
}
```

When the API returns **200** with an empty list, show no items (and ensure entries in Strapi have the tenant relation set). The only exception is the **400 Bad Request** fallback below (different endpoints, different reason).

## Published state filter

### DO: Use `filters[publishedAt][$notNull]=true`

```typescript
// ✅ DO: Filter for published documents
const query = `filters[publishedAt][$notNull]=true`;
```

### DON'T: Use `status=published`

```typescript
// ❌ DON'T: Can cause validation errors in Strapi 5
const query = `status=published`;
```

## Populate parameter (array-style)

### DO: Use array-style populate

```typescript
// ✅ DO: Array-style populate for Strapi 5
const POPULATE = 'populate[0]=cover&populate[1]=category&populate[2]=author';

// Full example
const path = `/articles?filters[tenant][tenantId][$eq]=${tenantId}&filters[publishedAt][$notNull]=true&populate[0]=cover&populate[1]=category&populate[2]=author&sort=publishedAt:desc&pagination[pageSize]=10`;
```

### DON'T: Use comma-separated populate

```typescript
// ❌ DON'T: Triggers 400 Bad Request in Strapi 5
const POPULATE = 'populate=cover,category,author';
```

### Exception: simple populate

For single-field populate (e.g. `populate=media`), the simple format may work. If you encounter 400s, switch to `populate[0]=media`.

## Example article query URLs

### Featured News (category slug — preferred)

```
GET /api/articles?filters[category][slug][$eq]=featured-news&filters[tenant][tenantId][$eq]=tenant_demo_002&filters[publishedAt][$notNull]=true&populate[0]=cover&populate[1]=category&populate[2]=author&sort=publishedAt:desc&pagination[pageSize]=6
```

### Featured News (`isFeatured` alternative)

```
GET /api/articles?filters[isFeatured][$eq]=true&filters[tenant][tenantId][$eq]=tenant_demo_002&filters[publishedAt][$notNull]=true&populate[0]=cover&populate[1]=category&populate[2]=author&sort=publishedAt:desc&pagination[pageSize]=6
```

### Main News / Press Release / Most Read

Same pattern with `filters[category][slug][$eq]=main-news` (or `press-release`, `most-read`), plus tenant + publishedAt + array populate.

**Category slugs:** prefer `$eq` with lowercase kebab-case after production slug backfill. Use `$eqi` only for legacy mixed-case data — see the slug contract rule.

## Article detail page (slug or id)

Detail routes accept slug, numeric id, or documentId:

1. **documentId** (first when param looks like documentId): `filters[documentId][$eq]=<documentId>` — alphanumeric 15–35 chars. Try documentId first when param matches `/^[a-z0-9]{15,35}$/`.
2. **Slug** (text): `filters[slug][$eq]=<slug>` — preferred for SEO (use `$eqi` only if legacy casing may remain).
3. **Numeric id** (e.g. `7`): `filters[id][$eq]=7` — when slug is empty.

Article links use: `article.slug || article.documentId || article.id`.

### Article not found: troubleshooting

When the API returns 200 but 0 items:

- **Try documentId first** when the URL param looks like a Strapi 5 documentId.
- **Tenant**: Article must have `tenant.tenantId` matching the app tenant. Do **not** retry without tenant.
- **publishedAt**: Article must be Published. Filter excludes drafts.

## Advertisement slots (sidebar + top)

```
filters[$or][0][position][$eq]=sidebar&filters[$or][1][position][$eq]=top
```

Split results client-side by `position`.

## Native Strapi 5 response format

Do **not** send `Strapi-Response-Format: v4`. Use native Strapi 5 flattened responses.

## Media / relation URL extraction (Strapi 4 vs 5)

Strapi 5 media URLs are no longer only at `relation.data.attributes.url`.

### DO: Helper that supports both formats

```typescript
function getMediaUrl(media: unknown, baseUrl: string): string | null {
  if (!media || !baseUrl) return null;
  const m = media as Record<string, unknown>;
  let url: string | undefined;
  url = m?.url as string | undefined;
  if (!url) url = (m?.data as Record<string, unknown>)?.url as string | undefined;
  if (!url) {
    const attrs = (m?.data as Record<string, unknown>)?.attributes as Record<string, unknown> | undefined;
    url = attrs?.url as string | undefined;
  }
  if (!url) return null;
  return url.startsWith('http') ? url : `${baseUrl}${url}`;
}
```

### DON'T: Assume only Strapi 4 structure

```typescript
// ❌ DON'T: Only handles Strapi 4
const url = media?.data?.attributes?.url;
```

Apply to: article `cover`, advertisement-slot `media`, promotional `thumbnail`.

## List endpoints: pagination and 400-only fallback

Use `pagination[page]=1` and `pagination[pageSize]=N` (not only `pagination[limit]=N`).

### DO: `pagination[pageSize]`

```typescript
'pagination[page]=1&pagination[pageSize]=1'
```

### 400-only fallback (not for 200 with 0 items)

Retry without tenant **only** when the request returns **400 Bad Request**. Never when 200 with empty data.

- **Articles, bishops, flash-news-items, advertisement-slots**: Always use tenant filter.
- **Exception**: Endpoints that return 400 with tenant + pagination (e.g. `catholicos-entries`) may try without tenant first for a narrow fallback (e.g. Catholicos image).

```typescript
const pathsToTry = [
  `catholicos-entries?pagination[pageSize]=1&populate[0]=image`,
  `catholicos-entries?filters[tenant][tenantId][$eq]=${encodeURIComponent(tenantId)}&pagination[pageSize]=1&populate[0]=image`,
];
let res: Response | null = null;
for (const path of pathsToTry) {
  res = await fetch(`${base}/${path}`, { headers: getStrapiHeaders(), cache: 'no-store' });
  if (res.ok) break;
}
```

